			F.carryZone, F.carryValue = nil, nil
			N.recoverDrop(carriedName)
			return true
		end
		-- Instant steal (owner 2026-11-02: "walk into the boss so its hit sends you to the safe zone with the animal"). The
		-- zone guard's catch flings the character (CatchFlingRemote "fling", velocity from the server, ZonesConfig.GuardFling
		-- 49693: FlingDistance 13 studs, capped by CarryLimits.MaxCarryFrom 22268 = land 25 studs short of the SafeZone edge),
		-- but the flight itself is client physics (CatchFlingController 77050-77079: Humanoid Physics state, the velocity is
		-- re-applied for 0.25 s, then free). So: with the animal, walk up to the zone guard, take the hit, and after the game's
		-- 0.25 s drive the ragdoll into the SafeZone (N.burstTo). Banked = Carrying cleared within 3 s of landing. Whether the
		-- hit leaves the animal in hand is the server's call (GuardMorphConfig.DropCarriedOnHit 23551 is the player-morph
		-- guard; live reports 2026-10-14/17 saw a zone guard drop it): carried=no on landing rejects the probe (steal_ride)
		-- and the normal recovery walk takes over.
		-- DORMANT (owner 2026-11-03, Discord ucupp "it teleports somewhere without the animal"): live on 2026-11-02 the guard's
		-- touch cleared Carrying before the fling every time, so this ride cost one animal per client before its probe
		-- rejected it. No toggle in the UI any more (a saved InstantSteal=true in a config is ignored: no toggle = on() false),
		-- the code stays behind this constant until a build where the carry survives the touch is seen.
